data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":1336,"output_index":5,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0b6d44bd578fa1ca016adb443832208191b0c07a9f3f8ca472","call_id":"call_645a3b0064f844a890af0962ee3c268b","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"aa6d2d87ccd3462d4aa5b7a25d9a2c1595a3653036998dfd2b71ae1ff55ca2cf\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review: the only mathematical task material read was packet.json, together with the declared Yui Audit A, self-containment, and format rules. Inputs are treated as conditional premises; this is not a source-fidelity review or carrier-identity/runtime attestation. The proof route is internally sufficient: the basis and divided-power calculations in S001 supply the characteristic-zero matrices; S002 obtains matrix units with coefficients invertible in Z_(p); S003 proves the coordinate module is a nonzero rank-one free module by explicit scalar-extension/dimension and localization arguments and the stated elementary ideal calculation; S004 transfers the basis and actions; S005–S008 prove irreducibility by the matrix-unit argument and close the zero/nonzero cases. I find no unsupported implication requiring external mathematical material.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"All cited inputs are the four listed hypotheses. Their parameter conditions and roles are used in the basis, localization, reduction, and module arguments; no unlisted source proposition is invoked.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The calculation and module-theoretic steps are given in the prose. In particular, the rank-one step does not assume J free: it computes the Q-dimension, embeds the torsion-free localization, clears denominators, and proves the resulting ideal is principal by the p-adic exponent calculation. The matrix-unit argument handles the endpoint and lambda=0 cases.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The factual uses are supported by listed H inputs, earlier local fact F001/F002/F003, definitions introduced in scope, or displayed calculations. The calculation-policy sentence is not needed as a substitute for the substantive S001–S007 arguments; no named external theorem is merely applied.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The conclusion is precisely that M tensor_Z K is nonzero and every invariant K-subspace under x,y,h is zero or the whole module. S004 establishes the basis correspondence, and S008 establishes both properties.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"W is introduced arbitrarily; L1 is confined to the nonzero branch, and F002/F003 and the chosen witnesses are used only there. The two cases establish the conclusion for the arbitrary W, and the positive dimension establishes nonzeroness.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/18\",\"/inference/locals/19\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/5\",\"/inference/argument/6\",\"/inference/argument/7\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"There are no E/M source inputs or source-theorem applications. The H inputs are applied at the stated parameter values; reduction uses p prime, characteristic p, and lambda<p.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input/output propositions state the relevant hypotheses and conclusion; the local proof spells out the basis, action formulas, coordinate modules, scalar-extension identifications, and invariant-subspace property rather than relying on theorem names or inherited references.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The mathematical objects used in the prose have packet declarations as parameters, primitives, input-bound objects, or local definitions/witnesses. The indexed matrix-unit occurrences are instances of the stated matrix-unit definition; witnesses a, w0, and i have the corresponding local existence bases.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/logic/primitives\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Reverse inspection of factual uses finds no ancestor-proof or ambient-H dependency: each substantive step is in this inference text, a listed H, or a previously produced local fact. S003's principal-ideal conclusion is supported by its explicit valuation argument, not a hidden PID citation.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/argument/2\",\"/inference/argument/3\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/5\",\"/inference/argument/6\",\"/inference/argument/7\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"I reviewed the complete frozen packet in this context with the declared procedure rules and no other mathematical task material. On that boundary, the packet suffices for the conditional proof. This judgment does not authenticate carrier identity, canonical-hash binding, transmission/readback, or runtime isolation beyond the supplied interaction.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/warning\",\"/inference/argument\"]}},\"findings\":[]}}","status":"completed"}}

