unit argument and close the zero/nonzero cases. I find no unsupported implication requiring external mathematical material.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"All cited inputs are the four listed hypotheses. Their parameter conditions and roles are used in the basis, localization, reduction, and module arguments; no unlisted source proposition is invoked.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The calculation and module-theoretic steps are given in the prose. In particular, the rank-one step does not assume J free: it computes the Q-dimension, embeds the torsion-free localization, clears denominators, and proves the resulting ideal is principal by the p-adic exponent calculation. The matrix-unit argument handles the endpoint and lambda=0 cases.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The factual uses are supported by listed H inputs, earlier local fact F001/F002/F003, definitions introduced in scope, or displayed calculations. The calculation-policy sentence is not needed as a substitute for the substantive S001–S007 arguments; no named external theorem is merely applied.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/argument/6/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The conclusion is precisely that M tensor_Z K is nonzero and every invariant K-subspace under x,y,h is zero or the whole module. S004 establishes the basis correspondence, and S008 establishes both properties.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"W is introduced arbitrarily; L1 is confined to the nonzero branch, and F002/F003 and the chosen witnesses are used only there. The two cases establish the conclusion for the arbitrary W, and the positive dimension establishes nonzeroness.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/18\",\"/inference/locals/19\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/5\",\"/inference/argument/6\",\"/inference/argument/7\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"There are no E/M source inputs or source-theorem applications. The H inputs are applied at the stated parameter values; reduction uses p prime, characteristic p, and lambda<p.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input/output propositions state the relevant hypotheses and conclusion; the local proof spells out the basis, action formulas, coordinate modules, scalar-extension identifications, and invariant-subspace property rather than relying on theorem names or inherited references.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The mathematical objects used in the prose have packet declarations as parameters, primitives, input-bound objects, or local definitions/witnesses. The indexed matrix-unit occurrences are instances of the stated matrix-unit definition; witnesses a, w0, and i have the corresponding local existence bases.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/logic/primitives\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/5/text\",\"/inference/